-- The Meridian Archive: the story of how this place came to be, told through
-- the documents left behind in Meridian Station. Players read the book in the
-- Lounge (the Archive window) and find the recovered files hidden around the
-- Garden. Pure data, shared by the server (which files exist) and the client
-- (which draws them).
--
-- Each document: id, title, kind (how it's typeset), meta (author, date or
-- source line), and blocks. A block is a paragraph string, or a table:
--   { heading = "..." }                      a small heading inside a document
--   { lines = { "...", "..." } }             monospace lines (logs, printouts)
--   { figure = "id", caption = "..." }       a picture (see Archive.Figures)
--   { signed = "..." }                       a signature line
-- Inline markup in any text: {{words}} is redacted (drawn as a black bar the
-- width of the words) and *words* is italic.
-- Kinds: "letter" (handwritten), "journal", "memo" (typewritten), "dossier",
-- "log" (terminal), "transcript", "report", "note".

local Archive = {}

Archive.Title = "The Meridian Archive"
Archive.Subtitle = "Recovered from Meridian Station. Reassembled and annotated by AJKR."

