	{
		id = "varga_journal",
		title = "First Light",
		kind = "journal",
		meta = "The personal journal of Dr. Ilse Varga, 1982 to 1984. Selected entries.",
		blocks = {
			{ heading = "4 June 1982" },
			"We began with cress. It's what you begin with when you don't know what you're doing and want to pretend you do. Trays at one metre, three metres, ten metres from the Lantern, everything else identical.",
			"At ten metres the cress grew like cress. At three metres it grew like it had somewhere to be. At one metre it grew into a shape. Not a random shape. A spiral, turning clockwise, every tray the same. When we rotated the tray, the spiral kept turning until it was facing the Lantern again.",
			{ figure = "exposure_chart", caption = "Growth against distance from the Lantern, first series. The curve is not a curve anyone has seen before." },
			{ heading = "19 August 1982" },
			"The Lantern responds to attention. I don't know how else to write it. If an observer watches it, its output rises. If two people watch it, it rises more. If the observers are afraid, it dims, slowly, the way you'd lower your voice in a room with a frightened animal.",
			"Toma from Physics says it's a feedback loop in the instruments, and I'd like that to be true, so I asked him to watch it with the instruments switched off. He came back after an hour, very pale, and asked to be moved to another project.",
			{ heading = "2 February 1983" },
			"The Board has approved human exposure. Volunteers only, strict limits, Medical present at all times. I argued for another year of plants and animals. I lost.",
			"I want it written down somewhere that I lost. If this goes wrong, I want the shape of my objection to survive me.",
			{ heading = "11 April 1983" },
			"The first volunteer stood in the light for ninety seconds. Afterward he walked out of the chamber, over to the loading dock, and lifted the front of a delivery truck off the ground with one hand, because, he said, he wanted to know if he could.",
			"He cried after. Not from pain. He said it felt like nothing. He said, *it felt like nothing at all, Doctor, and that's what scares me.*",
			{ heading = "30 October 1983" },
			"Each volunteer comes out different, and the difference isn't random. It isn't something the Lantern gives them. It's something it finds in them and turns up, like a dial. The strong man was always strong. The fencer was always half somewhere else. The engineer always talked to machines.",
			"So the question isn't what the Lantern does. The question is what it is looking for.",
			{ heading = "3 March 1984" },
			"I have stopped thinking of it as an object. Objects don't wait for you. I think it's a door. Or the light that comes under one.",
			"I think something on the other side is listening, and I think the light is how it learns what we are.",
			"I haven't told the Board. I don't know what I'd ask them to do about it.",
		},
