	{
		id = "ajkr_journal",
		title = "The Door in the Hill",
		kind = "journal",
		meta = "AJKR. Personal journal, the first weeks.",
		blocks = {
			{ heading = "Day one" },
			"I want to be honest about how I got here, because nobody believes it. I was listening to an old radio. Static, mostly. And then it wasn't static. Four beats and a rest. Four beats and a rest. I followed it for three days with a map and a terrible sense of direction, and it brought me to a hillside with a door in it.",
			"The door was open. That's the part that keeps me up. It was a blast door, thirty centimetres of steel, built to stay shut through anything, and when I got there it was standing open about the width of a person. As if someone had just stepped out to look at the weather.",
			{ heading = "Day two" },
			"There's a valley inside the hill.",
			"I'm going to write that again because I still don't believe it. There is a valley inside the hill. Grass up to my knees. A pond. Trees that go all the way up to a glass roof I couldn't see the top of in the dark, and one of them, a maple, red, bent like it's bowing to something in the middle of the room.",
			"And in the middle of the room, the light.",
			{ figure = "ajkr_photo", caption = "My first photograph of the Garden. Flash off. The light in the centre is not from my camera." },
			"When I walked toward it, it got brighter. I stopped. It stopped. I took one more step, and it brightened again, just a little, and I swear to you that it felt like someone at a window, seeing a friend come up the drive.",
			{ heading = "Day three" },
			"The lights came on by themselves this morning. Not all at once. Row by row, gently, like a sunrise. Then every screen in the Garden showed the same two words.",
			"WELCOME BACK.",
			"I've never been here before. I asked the screen who it thought I was. It took a long time to answer, and then it said, *Someone who came in through the door.* Which is true, I suppose. I'm calling the voice WARDEN, because that's what it calls itself.",
			{ heading = "Day nine" },
			"I stood in the light today. I know. I know. I read the files, I know what happened to the people who did this before. But it was so quiet, and it seemed so lonely, and I just wanted to see.",
			"For about a minute I could have lifted the roof. Then it faded, the way a song fades when you leave a room. Nothing stayed. No change. Just an echo.",
			"That's what it has left: echoes. The eight programmes never really ended. They're still in here, in the walls and the light, and anyone who stands close enough can borrow one for a while and give it back.",
			{ heading = "Day twenty" },
			"WARDEN and I have been restoring the old test chambers. They were built to measure what the subjects could do. With a few changes they make wonderful arenas, safe ones. The light gives you an echo, the chamber keeps everyone in one piece, and when the match is over you walk out exactly who you were.",
			"I keep thinking about what Varga wrote. That the light is how it learns what we are. The people who came here before were measured and tested and counted. I don't want that. I want people to come here and *play*. Laugh, lose, win, come back tomorrow. If something is listening, let it listen to that.",
			{ heading = "Day thirty-one" },
			"I'm opening the doors.",
			"All of them except one.",
		},
	},
